'' 'this' AS AN ARGUMENT IS THE OBJECT, not the pointer it is held in. Check typed it as
'' 'T ptr', so it was viable for no 'byref as T' or 'byval as T' parameter: a FUNCTION
'' call came out untyped and its statement was dropped -- starshine.bas's
'' 'this.ctr = getctr( This )' in a constructor -- and over 'byref as T' beside
'' 'byval as T ptr' the pointer overload was picked. Byval, lowering then passed the
'' pointer where the object's bytes belong. See the source.
''
'' MEASURED, fbc-modern 1.20, running the source:
''
''      6   7   8   10   20   0
''      2   3
''      42
''
'' -- byref, byval, default mode, 'ovl( this )' taking the byref T overload and
'' 'ovl( @this )' the pointer one; then the constructor's getctr; then a trivial type
'' byval ('BYV( *THIS$1 )' in fbc's C). tiko's build prints the same.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/this-arg-object.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: GETCTR(
'' EXPECT-OUT: call i32 BYR(
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN1TC1ERKS_(@$tmp
'' EXPECT-OUT: call i32 BYV(@$tmp
'' EXPECT-OUT: call i32 DFLT(
'' EXPECT-OUT: call i32 _Z3OVLR1T(
'' EXPECT-OUT: call i32 _Z3OVLP1T(
'' EXPECT-OUT: call i32 BYVU(
